%% F1 — out-of-DOM consent channel
%% See docs/04-patronus-guardian.md §4 and ADR-0006
sequenceDiagram
    participant Page as dApp page (DOM)
    participant Ext as Patronus Extension Surface
    participant Pat as Patronus Native App
    participant User
    participant DAG as L1 BlockDAG

    Page->>Ext: requestConsent(intent)
    Note over Page,Ext: Page may request, never render
    Ext->>Pat: deep-link / OS notification / URL scheme
    Pat-->>User: render dialog in Patronus's OWN UI surface
    Note right of User: DOM-level attackers cannot reach<br/>this surface (defeats V4 prompt spoofing,<br/>V5 XSS passkey substitution)

    alt user approves with hardware-backed authenticator (F2)
        User-->>Pat: approve
        Pat->>Pat: MDS3 check / Secure Enclave attest
        Pat-->>Ext: ConsentResult{ approved: true, consentRef }
        Ext-->>Page: yes + consentRef
    else user denies
        User-->>Pat: deny
        Pat->>DAG: emit AnomalyDetected (only if suspicious)
        Pat-->>Ext: ConsentResult{ approved: false, reason }
        Ext-->>Page: no + reason
    else page tries to render imitation dialog
        Pat->>DAG: emit AnomalyDetected("consent-channel-violation")
        Pat-->>Ext: error
    end
